      "writtenOn": "2025-10-28T04:21:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CONFIG_TEGRA_HSP_MBOX is essential for communication with BPMP in very-early kernel boot. If we build it as a module and load then the mbox is not available early on and so tegra bpmp cannot init and leads to failure for our device boot. Tegra bpmp driver also depends on TEGRA_HSP_MBOX enablement\n\nSpeaking of which, I missed that in the latest Linux kernel, Tegra bpmp is no longer selected by default by our arch config. Our Tegra BPMP is also critical for boot and needs to be enabled for our devices to boot. I\u0027ve updated the change to add that.",
      "parentUuid": "c28f6cde_41ba6270",
      "revId": "ffb98f95734dcc1ba93b1cbdc0d18444cc958bf6",
